  "Comparison Summary": "Both projects are nearly identical, sharing the same core strengths (clear rugged value prop for a real market, some development progress) and significant weaknesses (vague business model, lack of evidence, thin team details). Project B's only differentiator is the planned 3-year warranty. While this is a minor addition, it represents a tangible commitment to product quality and customer support that Project A omits. In crowdfunding, where backer trust is paramount, even a small, specific promise of post-purchase support can be a decisive factor. Therefore, Project B has a slight but meaningful edge."
}

